Learned counsel for the appellant/convict would further submit that the appellant/convict was of tender age of 20 years at the time of the alleged incident as it is evident from arrest memo (Exhibit Ka-9); that, the date of incident was 19.11.2018 and the prosecutrix was recovered on 23.11.2018 and her statement under Section 164 Cr.P.C. was recorded on 24.11.2018; that, the prosecutrix deviated from her statement recorded under Section 164 Cr.P.C. and the statement during her medical examination and stated before the Trial Court that the appellant/convict had taken her forcibly and sexually assaulted her; that, in her cross-examination, the prosecutrix/victim stated that she was under pressure of the appellant/convict when her statement under Section 164 Cr.P.C. was recorded, however, there was no question of any pressure from the appellant/convict as he was in jail at that time;
that, the appellant/convict himself is of tender age, that, concluding of the appeal would take long time, therefore, the appellant/convict may be granted bail.
6.
